sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Provider as Payment provider
    participant API as Callback endpoint
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant Worker as Settlement worker
    participant Client as Customer client
    Provider->>API: Callback with adapter-specific proof
    API->>API: Authenticate and normalize bounded payload
    API->>DB: Persist unique inbox event
    DB-->>API: Durable acceptance or existing duplicate
    API-->>Provider: Acknowledge accepted event
    Worker->>DB: Lease pending inbox event
    opt Callback needs authoritative provider query
        Worker->>Provider: Query same transaction reference
        Provider-->>Worker: Merchant, amount, currency and result
    end
    Worker->>DB: BEGIN, lock order, payment and stock records
    alt Event already applied
        Worker->>DB: No-op and COMMIT
    else Verified capture with active hold
        Worker->>DB: Capture fact, reserve to allocate, order pending
        Worker->>DB: Summary, financial event and outbox, COMMIT
    else Verified capture after release or cancellation
        Worker->>DB: Capture fact, payment exception, refund task
        Worker->>DB: No fulfillment revival, COMMIT
    else Invalid financial match or illegal transition
        Worker->>DB: Record rejection or incident, COMMIT
    end
    Client->>API: Fetch order after provider redirect
    API->>DB: Read authorized durable state
    API-->>Client: Pending, paid or exception state
    Note over Client,DB: Redirect parameters never establish payment success
